# Luxonis OAK — udev rules for the score depth-camera backend.
#
# depthai-core talks to the camera over raw USB through XLink, so without these
# the device nodes stay root-owned, discovery returns nothing, and the symptom
# is indistinguishable from nothing being plugged in.
#
# 03e7 is Movidius, the vendor id every OAK enumerates under. It covers both
# states an OAK passes through, and that is why the rule is vendor-wide rather
# than per-product: an unbooted device shows one product id (2485, the ROM
# bootloader) and a running one another (f63b), so a product-specific rule
# grants access to a camera that has already been opened and not to the one you
# are trying to open. Luxonis' own 80-movidius.rules is vendor-wide for the
# same reason.
#
# Ethernet models need no rule at all — they are reached over TCP, not USB.
#
# Deliberately no ACTION!="add" guard: `udevadm trigger` fires *change* events
# by default, so an add-only rule silently does nothing until the camera is
# physically replugged.

SUBSYSTEM!="usb", GOTO="score_depthai_end"

ATTR{idVendor}=="03e7", MODE="0666", TAG+="uaccess"

LABEL="score_depthai_end"
